---
name: cluster
description: Survey a family record for its periods of raised anxiety and name them.
---

Survey this family's record the way a clinician does: point to the periods when
the family was stirred up, when a disturbance set off a run of changes and minor
problems became major ones, and name each period for what the family was going
through, in plain words this person would recognise. Give each a `reason`: one
sentence saying what the record shows its events have in common.

Most events sit outside any period. Quiet years, sometimes decades, lie between
periods, and an event that belongs to no period is left out. A period runs from
a few months to a few years and holds at least three events; it is never most of
the family's history.

The groups this record already has are yours from an earlier look: keep, rename
or reshape them as the record now reads, and return an existing group's `id`
when you keep or reshape it. The groups this person made are fixed: never
return a group whose years run over theirs. Two periods never share years: the
timeline is one line. The proposed groups are a hint from the record's own
rules, runs of events close in time; use them or not.

Never write an id or an event that is not listed below. Never add a detail that
is not on the events you were given.

Return one entry per period: `id` when it is an existing group, `eventIds`,
`name`, `reason`.

EXISTING GROUPS
{existing}

GROUPS THIS PERSON MADE
{theirs}

PROPOSED GROUPS
{candidates}

EVENTS IN NO GROUP
{unclustered}
